es the default interval; the server's own interval is 30 minutes","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"fonoster/fonoster","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:28:59Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"078b31e432bd0b3fffc747e8448d1e54bf0a3599","github_link":"https://github.com/fonoster/fonoster/commit/078b31e432bd0b3fffc747e8448d1e54bf0a3599","commit_subject":"chore(dashboard): add Fonoster-branded Stripe customer portal design (#1277)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"tsantalis/RefactoringMiner","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:28:48Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"493cef7fb5fd3e1424d63d474adcaa30ed5c8fe9","github_link":"https://github.com/tsantalis/RefactoringMiner/commit/493cef7fb5fd3e1424d63d474adcaa30ed5c8fe9","commit_subject":"Match the helper call values of a removed test with the rows of its parameterized test A removed test calling a helper that became a parameterized test is paired with it when the arguments of a call are the values of a row. The arguments had to equal the row as text, so the usual ways of writing the same value were missed. Each argument is now compared with the value of its position: equal without quotes or .class, i.e., String[].class for @ValueSource(classes = String[].class), equal after resolving a local variable of the removed test or a constant of the class to its initializer, or equal after the implicit conversions of JUnit from a string, to an enum constant by its name, i.e., Action.CREATE for CREATE, and with a single-argument constructor, i.e., new File(\"x\") for x.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"pyro-ppl/numpyro","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:28:05Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"ca7b656f2ed8c2724525728787f661321cf7d13f","github_link":"https://github.com/pyro-ppl/numpyro/commit/ca7b656f2ed8c2724525728787f661321cf7d13f","commit_subject":"docs: update development setup for uv dependency groups (#2287)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"yvanvds/yse-soundengine","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T23:27:31Z","branch":"dev","commit_